d-power actions; the matrix-unit constructions use the indicated unit binomial coefficients; the localization argument establishes rank-one freeness of J; and reduction and matrix units yield the invariant-subspace conclusion. I find no unsupported mathematical implication in these calculations under the packet's explicit finite-matrix, localization, and free-module-reduction calculation allowance. This judgment does not cure the separate missing declaration of w.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\",\"/inference/argument/4/text\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The factual grounds used in the prose are the direct H inputs, the earlier locally produced F001, and the stated elementary calculations. The author-written calculation policy is not being treated as a license for unrelated theorems; the indicated computations are the specified matrix, localization, and free-module reduction work. No E/M theorem application or unlisted substantive theorem is invoked.\",\"locations\":[\"/logic/calculations/0\",\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/1\",\"/inference/argument/2\",\"/inference/argument/3\",\"/inference/argument/4\",\"/inference/applications\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"S005's conclusion is exactly that the module is nonzero and every invariant K-subspace under x,y,h is zero or the whole module. The argument establishes the nonzero case via matrix units and states positive dimension, including the lambda=0 endpoint. The missing w declaration is an object-closure defect rather than a different output statement.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/4/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"S005's coordinate argument invokes a chosen nonzero w in W and coefficients c_i, but the local declarations contain no w and no existential witness declaration for such a vector. Thus the chosen object/coordinate argument is not explicitly scoped or grounded in the packet. The proof does not make this a declared local witness or spell out a case/quantifier closure establishing the nonzero-subspace case from the conditional argument.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/4/text\",\"/inference/locals\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"There are no external or mathlib propositions and no source-theorem applications. The four H inputs are used with compatible parameters and stated ranges; F001 is used after its local derivation in S003.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/applications\",\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/argument/2/produces/0\",\"/inference/argument/3\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The packet gives complete direct input and target statements and supplies the full basis, operator, coordinate-module, and scalar-extension content used in the argument. There is no dependence on an original equation number or another inference's proof body. The undeclared w is handled under object/scope closure, not as missing statement text.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs\",\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/4/text\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Reverse-checking the actual prose finds w in S005 ('If w=... is nonzero in W') and a coordinate expansion in the b-basis, but no local declaration for w. The c_i declaration is conditional on 'the chosen nonzero w' and does not itself introduce or prove existence of w. A nonzero witness cannot be supplied by its appearance in the prose.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/4/text\",\"/inference/locals/22\",\"/inference/locals\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Apart from the object/scope defect already recorded, factual steps map to direct H inputs, the earlier F001, or explicit elementary calculations. No ancestor proof or unlisted proposition is needed for the inspected algebraic claims.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/1\",\"/inference/argument/2\",\"/inference/argument/3\",\"/inference/argument/4\",\"/inference/argument/2/produces/0\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Sufficiency judged from this packet alone: it is not sufficient for a closed replay of the full inference because the S005 nonzero vector w is used without a declaration or witness basis. The actual mathematical-material boundary was packet.json plus the declared Yui review rules. Carrier identity and canonical hash binding are outside this mathematical judgment; I do not claim runtime attestation or a separate carrier-level freshness certificate.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/4/text\",\"/inference/locals\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"/inference/argument/4/text\",\"finding\":\"S005 uses a chosen nonzero vector w in W, expands it in the b-basis, and uses its coefficients, but no local declaration or witness introduction for w exists. The coordinate-coefficient declaration at /inference/locals/22 presupposes that missing object.\",\"effect\":\"object_closure and scope fail; packet_replay cannot pass on packet sufficiency.\"}]}}"}

